# Splunk Threat Hunting Queries (SPL)

Below is the Search Processing Language (SPL) utilized during the threat hunting phase to filter noise, extract indicators of compromise (IOCs), and build visual timeline metrics.

### 1. Threat Intelligence Extraction
**Isolate Top 5 Malicious Source IPs:**
```spl
index=* status="Failed"
| top limit=5 src_ip
| rename src_ip as "Malicious Source IP", count as "Attack Attempts", percent as "Share of Traffic %"
```

**Identify Top Targeted User Accounts:**
```spl
index=* status="Failed"
| top limit=5 user
| rename user as "Targeted Credential", count as "Failed Guesses"
```

### 2. Timeline & Pattern Analysis
**Map Attack Frequency by Hour (Timecharting):**
```spl
index=* | eval hour=strftime(strptime(timestamp, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S"), "%H")
| stats count by hour
| sort hour
```

**Extract Specific Attacker Timestamps (IP Tracking):**
```spl
index=* src_ip="45.33.32.156"
| sort timestamp
| table timestamp, user, status
| rename timestamp as "Time", user as "User", status as "Result"
```

### 3. Baseline & Demographic Monitoring
**Compare Overall Authentication Status (Failed vs. Accepted):**
```spl
index=*| stats count by status
```

**Map Attack Origins Geographically:**
```spl
index=* status="Failed"
| iplocation src_ip
| geostats count by Country
```

**Audit Successful Logins for Lateral Movement:**
```spl
index=* status="Accepted"
| table timestamp, user, src_ip, hostname
```
